00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.780
The size of the mini infinity firework depends on the paper you use. If you want a larger

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:49.559
one you can use 11 by 17 inch paper or
you can also use eight-and-a-half by 14

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:52.680
legal sized
to get a mid sized one however if you

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.789
want a cool mini hand size one you can
use eight-and-a-half by 11 letter sized

00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:00.329
paper like this one.  I prefer to use the
color paper because it's slightly

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:03.719
sturdier than white and I find it works
better so that's what I'm going to use

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:07.170
We're going to first turn the
8.5" by 11" into a 1-to-4

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:11.189
proportion paper, make all the pre
creases and finally once we get this

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:16.140
accordion thing, we can then take the two
ends and we can join them together just

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.780
like this in order to get the mini
infinity firework.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.720
To get a 1:4 proportion paper like this we need to
first divide the paper into four

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:30.750
sections. Now, I've already pre-creased
this one but to do it we first fold the

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:34.079
paper in half by taking the left side
and folding it to the right side and

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:38.280
then rotate it so the open edges are on
top. Take the top edge fold it down and

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.759
then flip it over and do the same. Crease
it sharply and when you open it'll look

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:46.979
like an M from the side. Airplane fold
both corners in just like this and at

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:49.829
this point if you want to take a ruler
and draw a line at the base of the

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:53.909
corner triangles and cut it you can but
I prefer to flip it over like this fold

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:57.450
the top edge down until the edge is in
line with the triangles, and then make a

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:01.990
nice sharp crease on the top there and
then you could tear it

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:06.820
Now you have a 1 to 4 proportion
paper. The next step is going to be to

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:11.700
split it into 8 sections just like this
I'm going to draw on the center just so

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.360
you could see it a little bit easier
because it does become important.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.280
To split it into 8 sections we're going to
take this line here in between these two

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.700
right boxes and we're going to just
pinch it like this

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:29.200
and we're going to bring it directly
into the middle line just like that and

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.200
what that does is it splits this box in
half so let's go ahead and do that.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:37.700
Just pinch it bring it into the middle right
on top of that line I drew and then

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:42.400
you're going to press in the middle of
this right box here. So just press right

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.319
down here.  Then we can take the outside
edge and also fold it directly into the

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:51.700
middle. Once it's there then once again
make a crease do the same with the left side

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:55.239
So just pinch the left side
bring it into the center also and then

00:02:55.239 --> 00:02:58.840
crease it on the left box and then fold
the left edge into the center and crease

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:03.190
both sides sharply. When you open it
you'll see we've now split the paper

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:06.820
into eight sections and I'm just going
to draw on them so you can see them a

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:11.720
little easier because they become
important when we make the diagonal folds

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:16.060
Now that we split the paper into
eight sections it's important that I

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:21.609
emphasize that all of the vertical folds
must be Mountain folds meaning we're

00:03:21.609 --> 00:03:26.680
going to fold downwards on each of these
folds so let's go ahead and do that now

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.280
So let's just fold downwards on all of
them and crease across. I've also marked

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:34.810
the center line as darker so that it's
easier to distinguish and what we're

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:39.220
going to do is to turn this into
something that looks like this. It has

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:45.130
eight sections and each section has two
X's on top of each other. To do that

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.760
we're going to start with the diagonal
folds going this direction and then

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.660
we're going to go in this direction. We're going to first take the corner

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:57.819
here and we're going to take this top
edge and fold the corner into this first

00:03:57.819 --> 00:04:02.290
line just like this. Once it's lined up
then you can make a crease on the

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:06.790
outside, then we're going to go to the
second line in so this one has already

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:10.479
been made so all you need to do is to
fold it down and just reinforce it by

00:04:10.479 --> 00:04:15.490
sharpening it then we're going to go to
the third one just go right there line

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:20.110
and make sure that this line on the
bottom also corresponds with the bottom

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:24.520
as well so that everything is lined up.
Make a nice sharp crease and then

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:29.710
finally go in directly to the center
line here. Once it's lined up again make

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:35.170
a crease. Now we could flip it over just
like this and we're going to do the same

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:39.790
with the upper right so just like before
go to the first line the second line the

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:44.830
third line and then finally the center. When you open it up you'll see that

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:49.750
we did all of them except one from here
to here. What you do is you just take

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:54.910
it fold it down to the center and then
just shift this edge over to the next

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:59.200
line to the left of the center.  So just
shift it over and crease like before.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:03.610
Now we finished all of the diagonal
lines going this way and I'm just going

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:09.580
to draw on them so you could see it a
little bit easier.  Now we're going to do

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.750
the same going the other way so we're
going to take the upper left corner and

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:19.450
fold it in to the first line also just
like this make a nice sharp crease and

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.390
it's basically the same thing. We're
going to fold it all the way to the

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:26.080
middle just like before so just like
before just go to the second, one the

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.500
third one, and then the middle. You
flip it over do the same thing bring the

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:33.070
upper left down to each line and then
finally when you get to the middle just

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:38.170
open one up and then shift it over give
it a nice crease and now we finished all

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.680
of the diagonal creases and I'm just
going to draw on the remaining ones

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:47.740
again so you could see them easier. So
you should have a paper that looks just

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.310
like this. Alright guys so we're almost
done we just need to divide the eight

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:56.800
sections into 16 sections vertically and
then we can create something like this

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:00.310
and join it together. You already know
what to do you just basically bring

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.540
these edges into the center until we
have split everything into 16 sections

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:08.860
so let's go ahead and do that just pinch
it here and bring it into the center and

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:13.330
then make a crease right along here and
just keep on bringing the edges into the

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:17.200
center just like that so just keep
bringing those Mountain folds into the

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:21.790
center until you have split everything
into 16 sections and each of those X's

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:25.720
has a vertical line through it and then
we can reinforce the creases by just

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.600
going over the outside and do the same
with

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:33.310
other side. Now we can open it and you'll
see we've divided everything into 16

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:36.460
sections. Now this is very important--We
need to make sure that all of these

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:41.740
vertical folds are Mountain folds so I'm
going to hold it like this and I'm just

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:47.320
going to fold downwards or backwards
like this so that all of the folds are

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:51.130
folded downwards so just like before
we're going to crease downwards on all

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:55.060
of those vertical lines and making sure
that they're all nice sharp mountain

00:06:55.060 --> 00:07:04.900
folds just continue throughout the rest
of the paper now that we've done that

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:10.960
I'm just going to reinforce that all of
the diagonal folds are valley folds so

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.910
just take it and then just push it and
then go through all of the folds this is

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.660
very important it makes it 10 times
easier trust me so I'm just taking the

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:24.160
paper and just going back over those X
folds or diagonal Valley folds we made.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:27.760
Now that we finished all the pre creases
we can make it into this and then finish

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:31.690
up by joining the ends. Alright,
everyone once you've reinforced all of

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:36.700
these vertical fold mountain creases so
they're folded downwards sharply so that

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:40.240
they look like an upside-down V and
you've gone through that throughout the

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:45.670
whole paper and you've also done all of
